# NOTHING THAT COULD CARRY DATA. The image is the tool; an
# extract or a run directory swept into a layer would travel
# with every pull of it, which is the worst possible way for a
# record to leave an account.
data/
*.csv
*.parquet
*.xlsx
run_*/
.venv*/
.git/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# AND NOTHING THAT THE TEAM BUNDLE ALREADY REFUSES TO SHIP.
#
# `make_team_bundle.py` keeps an EXCLUDE_FILES list for the
# filtered export: the lab notebook, the sprint board, the
# runbooks that carry a machine's real paths, the demo scripts and
# the personal scanner that contains the patterns it scans for.
# An image that may run in a hospital's own AWS account is a
# second way out of this repo, and it had no such list at all.
#
# THIS DUPLICATES THAT LIST, WHICH THAT FILE ALREADY CALLS A KNOWN
# RISK - "if this list changes, that file must change with it".
# There are now three copies (bundle, operator export, here). A
# single source of truth would be better and is named as owed.
RUNBOX.md
RUNBOX.html
CONVENTIONS.md
docs/SPRINT.md
docs/WINDOWS.md
docs/DEMO_LLM_WINDOWS.md
docs/demo_script.md
docs/demo_script_v2.md
docs/demo_script_clinic.md
docs/demo_prompt.md
# An internal working note addressed to a named colleague. Fine
# in the repo and fine in the team bundle, which goes to people in
# this organisation; not something to ship in an image that may
# run in an account outside it.
docs/RAI_EVIDENCE_INDEX.md
